[FINAL-TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: sshswitch
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: Layer-3 SVI for Campus 2 VLAN 6 on sshswitch (interface br_v6). Mechanism: PCs in VLAN 6 ARP for their configured default gateway 10.6.0.254 but receive no reply because the actual gateway IP on the VLAN 6 SVI is set to 10.6.0.200. As a result, hosts cannot resolve 10.6.0.254 and traffic to off-subnet destinations fails, while intra-VLAN traffic continues to work.

Localization: 
- On pc3/pc4, default route is via 10.6.0.254, and ARP for 10.6.0.254 shows “FAILED/incomplete,” yet they can ping 10.6.0.200 (the SVI on sshswitch) and each other (10.6.0.3/10.6.0.4), confirming L2 is healthy. 
- On sshswitch, br_v6 is configured with 10.6.0.200/24, whereas other SVIs follow the .254 convention (e.g., br_v5 = 10.5.0.254).

Root cause: The VLAN 6 SVI on sshswitch was misconfigured with IP 10.6.0.200/24 instead of the documented gateway 10.6.0.254/24.

Corrective fix: Reassign the correct gateway address to the VLAN 6 SVI on sshswitch. Example: remove 10.6.0.200/24 from br_v6 and add 10.6.0.254/24 (and update the switch’s persistent config). After updating, verify ARP resolution from pc3/pc4 (ip neigh) and confirm ping to 10.6.0.254 succeeds. No changes are required on switch4 or end hosts if they were already pointing to 10.6.0.254. === END ===